A||||3||Jeff Blowers||Check Engine Light||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff Blowers||10-31-2001||08:36 PM||||My check engine light came on last night.  Once I got home, and re-started the car it was no longer coming on.  Does anyone know if the code is stored so that I can read it (last code recorded) if the light is not on?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-31-2001||08:45 PM||||Yes, any and all codes should be in there unless it has been cleared out by disconnecting its power source. Even if they have been read and the ECM has not been reset, the codes will remain.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jeff Blowers||10-31-2001||09:01 PM||||Thanks for the answer on that.  That makes sense.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-31-2001||09:16 PM||||Any particular code is cleared after 50 starts without that code occurring again.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
